article:
Whereas, God in His wisdom has seen best to remove from our midst Mrs. Lou. J. Brown, a member of the Woman's Mis-. sionary Society of the Presby- terian Church of Prescott, Ark, Therefore, be it resolved;

 That, in her going, the Society loses one of its most faithful and Jealous members and that we cherish her memory and rejoice in the hope that she has entered into that rest prepared for all those who love the Lord;

 That we extend to her family our sympathy in their bereave- ment and assure them of our prayers, that the Holy Spirit may be given them;

 That copy of these resolu- tions be sent to the family of the deceased, to the Christian Ob. server ard Daily News and that they be spread upon the records of our Society.

 Com mmittpp

article_spellcheck:
Whereas, God in His wisdom has seen best to remove from our midst Mrs. Lou. J. Brown, a member of the Woman's Missionary Society of the Presbyterian Church of Prescott, Ark, Therefore, be it resolved;

That, in her going, the Society loses one of its most faithful and zealous members and that we cherish her memory and rejoice in the hope that she has entered into that rest prepared for all those who love the Lord;

That we extend to her family our sympathy in their bereavement and assure them of our prayers, that the Holy Spirit may be given them;

That a copy of these resolutions be sent to the family of the deceased, to the Christian Observer and Daily News and that they be spread upon the records of our Society.

Committee
